From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wbemprox: Win32_ProcessStartup and Win32_Process.Create ProcessStartupInformation (3681)

wbemprox: Win32_ProcessStartup and Win32_Process.Create ProcessStartupInformation

Win32_ProcessStartup is a class now (CreateFlags, EnvironmentVariables,
ErrorMode, FillAttribute, PriorityClass, ShowWindow, Title, WinstationDesktop,
X, Y, XSize, YSize, XCountChars, YCountChars) and Win32_Process.Create has the
ProcessStartupInformation object parameter. An uncommitted instance can hold
an embedded object (CIM_OBJECT: Put keeps a copy, Get returns a copy). Create
applies the startup information to CreateProcess: window position, size,
character counts, fill attribute, ShowWindow, title, desktop, creation and
priority flags, and the environment variables.
